'''Marquis Clionius''' (クオリネス卿, ''Kuorinesu Kyō'', '''Lord Kuoliness''') is an [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of [[Cruel Angel Clionel]] that appears in [[Zero Legends]]. They were introduced in [[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Marquis Clionius
|image = E 786.png
|first appearance = '''ZL:''' [[Pipette of Passion|Sub-chapter 35 - Pipette of Passion]]
|money drop = 5,000¢ - 19,750¢
}}

==Enemy==
Marquis Clionius is a [[Long Distance]] backliner that works much like [[Cruel Angel Clionel]], but is more oriented towards support, dealing less damage and replacing [[Slow]] with a guaranteed 25% [[Drain]] and 68% uptime [[Freeze]]. Although their health is lower than Clionel's, they balance it out with a powerful [[Shield]] and [[Explosion Immunity]], making rushing with cats like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] less viable.

==Strategy==
Marquis Clionius' [[Shield]] more than doubles their effective HP unless [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|pierced]] every time, so high-speed Shield Piercers like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Cow Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Lion Cat]], [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]], [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]], [[Hajime Saito (Uber Rare Cat)|Hajime Saito]] and [[Inosuke Hashibira (Uber Rare Cat)|Inosuke Hashibira]] are recommended. [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] is a perfect choice of [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshield]], stalling Marquis Clionius very effectively with its [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] [[Resistant|Resistance]] and [[Immune to Freeze|Freeze Immunity]].

In spite of Clionius' [[Immune to Explosions|Explosion Immunity]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] is still a good counter, easily able to rush into Clionius' blind spot and deal a lot of damage. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]] can even use Clionius as a stepping stone akin to [[Johnnyleon]], utilizing outer [[Explosion|Explosions]] to hit the supporting peons behind Clionius. Besides Bahamut, [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] (with the usage of stepping stones) can help sneak in damage too. If Clionius' [[Freeze]] and [[Drain]] are giving you trouble, you can use [[Brainwashed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Lion Cat]] when their Shield is inactive to disable these effects.

In some stages, such as [[Distilled Devotion]], you will not have a clear path to Clionius. In this case, you might have to lure the enemy pushers away from Clionius to isolate them, taking advantage of Clionius's slow speed.

