==Trivia==
*''Marquis'' is French for [[wikipedia:Marquess|marquess]], a nobleman ranked higher than a count, but lower than a duke. The female equivalent is ''marquise''.
*The name Clionius may be derived from ''[[wikipedia:Clione|clione]]'' and ''genius''.
*Marquis Clionius' Japanese name, Kuorinesu Kyō (クオリネス卿), can be taken as "Lord Kuolines", "Lord Kuorines", "Lord Kuoliness", "Lord Kuoriness", "Lord Kuolineth", or "Lord Kuorineth", which may be a combination of クリオネ ''kurione'' (clione) and ''business'', ''demoness'', ''highness'', ''unholiness'', ''unruliness'', ''villainess'', or ''[[wikipedia:Lilith|Lilith]]'' (リリス ''Ririsu''), as Clionius going from its home world to [[The Aku Realms]] and having three Aku children may parallel Lilith leaving the Garden of Eden and having many demonic children. Its debut sub-chapter appears to be about an obsessive person trying to force someone else into loving them and only them (see [[Yandere Chemistry#Trivia]] for more information), which could reference portrayals of Lilith as a succubus who seduces or even forces herself onto men, as in the [[wikipedia:Zohar|Zohar]]. Fitting with [[Cruel Angel Clionel]]'s ''[[wikipedia:Neon Genesis Evangelion|Neon Genesis Evangelion]]'' references, [https://wiki.evageeks.org/Lilith Lilith] is also a creature in the show.
**Clionius' first two stages, [[Pipette of Passion]] and [[Distilled Devotion]], contain [[Sinner Snache]], while Lilith has been associated with serpents, such as in ''[[wikipedia:Sistine Chapel ceiling#Adam and Eve|The Fall and Expulsion from Paradise]]'' on the Sistine Chapel ceiling, where the serpent in the Garden of Eden appears to be depicted as Lilith, and John Collier's painting ''[[wikipedia:Lilith (painting)|Lilith]]'', which shows a serpent coiled around her body.
**Clionius was added in [[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]] alongside [[Lilith Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Queen Succubus Cat]]'s [[Talents]], which make her immune to Clionius' Freeze and immune to the [[Death Surge]]s from the peons in Clionius' first two stages. In [[BCEN]], Queen Succubus Cat's Normal Form is even named Lilith Cat.
*Besides the above, Marquis Clionius' Japanese name could also be derived from the following goetic demons:
**Marquis [[wikipedia:Forneus|Forneus]] (フォルネウス ''Foruneusu''), who teaches rhetoric and languages. Forneus is depicted as a great sea monster, and Clionius is a giant clione.
**Marquis [[wikipedia:Orias|Orias]] (オリアス ''Oriasu''), who teaches astrology.
**Marquis [[wikipedia:Kimaris|Kimaris/Cimeries]] (キメリエス ''Kimeriesu''), who can locate lost or hidden treasures and teaches grammar, logic and rhetoric.
**Presidents [[wikipedia:Foras|Foras]] (フォラス ''Forasu'') and [[wikipedia:Morax (demon)|Morax]] (モラクス ''Morakusu''), both of whom grant knowledge of all herbs and precious stones. Morax appears as a man-headed bull or bull-headed man, which might be referenced by Clionius' horns, and Morax's name seems to come from the Latin word ''mora'', meaning "delay" or "duration of time", which correlates with Clionius' Drain and Freeze abilities.
*Marquis Clionius' wealth may reference [[wikipedia:Clauneck|Clauneck]], a goetic demon of wealth, or the biblical [[wikipedia:King Solomon|King Solomon]], an extremely wise and wealthy king of ancient Israel whose indulgence and lust led to idolatry and thence his punishment by the God he turned away from. In the [[wikipedia:Testament of Solomon|Testament of Solomon]], he brings demons under his control, which may be represented by the demonic children who attack in unison with Clionius.
*The rift in space and time in Marquis Clionius' description may be the [[Media:Rc149.png|purple portal]] that appears in [[Dimension Rift]], [[Spacetime Distortion]] and some other stages with [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]], or the [[Media:Rc172.png|red wormhole]] that appears in [[Zero Legends]]' [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cat]] stages.
*The text that appears when Marquis Clionius attacks is flipped katakana in the Aku writing system that translates to "cute children".

